# An allowlist: the build context holds only these paths, so nothing else
# in the working tree (the root data directory, private fixtures, editor
# files) can reach an image layer, not even an intermediate one.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!api/
!cmd/
!internal/
!web/

# Within them: dependencies are installed and the web app is built inside
# the image, and no data or secrets go in, at any depth (a server started
# from a subdirectory puts its data directory there).
**/node_modules
internal/webui/dist
web/codegen
web/coverage
**/data
**/testdata/private
**/.env*
**/.npmrc
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite*
**/*.tmp
**/*.test
**/coverage.out
